[268.203, "o", "{\"advice\":\"Rahim, for your elevated blood glucose and high screening risk, a simple weekly plan: Meals should be half vegetables and fruit, a quarter whole grains, and a quarter protein. Examples: oats with fruit and boiled egg for breakfast; brown rice with vegetables and grilled fish or tofu for lunch; clear vegetable soup with lean protein and a smaller rice portion for dinner. Drinks: water or less sweet tea. For exercise, do indoor morning sessions: warm up 5-10 mins with light marching and stretches; moderate aerobic activity like mall walking 20-30 mins; strength exercises 2 days/week like sit-to-stand and wall push-ups; balance exercises daily; cool down with stretches. Keep intensity moderate, stop if you feel unwell, and check with your doctor before starting. This fits your age, glucose status, hazy region, and preference for indoor morning activity.\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"supporting_guides\":[\"lg-01-healthy-plate\",\"lg-05-eating-for-pre-diabetes\",\"lg-06-exercise-by-condition\",\"lg-09-hazy-day-activity\",\"lg-10-active-after-60\"],\"rationale\":\"The plan follows LiveWell guide recommendations tailored to Rahim's age (60-64), elevated blood glucose, high screening risk, preference for indoor and morning exercise, and regional haze conditions. The meal plan emphasizes balanced carbs and protein for glucose control, while the exercise plan includes aerobic, strength, balance, and flexibility safe for his condition.\",\"personalisation_flags\":[\"age_60-64\",\"condition_elevated b...\r\n"]
