[336.688, "o", "{\"advice\":\"For managing pre-diabetes, build meals around fibre and balance. Choose wholegrains more often like brown rice or wholemeal bread. Use the healthy plate pattern: half vegetables and fruit, one quarter wholegrains or staples, and one quarter protein foods such as fish, chicken, tofu, or eggs. Spread carbohydrates evenly through the day and avoid skipping meals. Swap sugary drinks for water, unsweetened tea, or kopi siew dai. Watch portions using your hand as a guide: a palm-sized protein portion, a fist-sized staple portion, and two handfuls of non-starchy vegetables. Avoid crash diets and speak to a doctor for personalized advice.\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"supporting_guides\":[\"lg-05-eating-for-pre-diabetes\",\"lg-01-healthy-plate\",\"lg-04-salt-and-sugar-tips\"],\"rationale\":\"This advice specifically fits your high screening risk due to elevated blood glucose and aims to manage pre-diabetes by encouraging steady, balanced eating habits with sensible carbohydrate portions and healthier drink options.\",\"personalisation_flags\":[\"high_screening_risk\",\"elevated_blood_glucose\"]}\r\n"]
